# Logs
*.log

# sources/ and library/ are intentionally tracked (pinned upstream trees and
# curated Library copies) — do not add ignore rules for them here.
#
# The generic rules above (*.log, node_modules/, dist/, build/, __pycache__/, ...)
# match at every depth, so without these negations they silently strip files out
# of a Source tree that is supposed to be committed verbatim at its pinned
# Revision — which would make Change review diff against a corrupted baseline.
# These re-include everything under both trees; the negations must stay last.
!/sources/**
!/library/**

# Pre-migration recovery snapshot: 113M of tarballs plus 6 embedded upstream
# clones (which git would turn into phantom gitlinks — empty on every clone).
# It's a local safety net, not source of truth; sources/ holds the tracked trees.
backups/

# Skima local machine state: `skima check` writes .skima/status.json on
# demand from sources.json + a live `git ls-remote`, so it's ephemeral and
# per-machine, not source of truth. sources.json itself stays tracked.
.skima/
